const INFO = "An informational record (an overlap / apply-order / boundary note for that wave's integrator); integrated since — every later wave pushed on the chain's GUARD_EXIT=0. Nothing to do in code."
const SUPERSEDED = "A status line of that wave's lane report (what was not run or still red at that moment); superseded by each later integrated gate (sweep + whole-project tsc + GUARD_EXIT=0). Nothing to close in code."
const DOCS = "Generated-doc / baseline / cache regeneration for the integrator after merge (operations-docs --write, feature-certification --write-doc, orphan / cron baselines, TEST-MATRIX, READINESS-MATRIX). Each wave's integrator regenerates them; no repo state proves one past regeneration, so it stays the integrator's standing chore — not a code defect."
const CANARY = "A canary REQUIREMENT (the behaviour that wave's canary lane was asked to drive), not an open defect; executed by that wave's canary runner, which is chained."
const OWNERQ = "An owner / product decision the lane recorded and did not invent; the code holds the conservative reading until the owner rules. Still undecided at 08712fef."
